/admin/users
/admin/resources
/admin/projects
/admin/events
/admin/opportunities
/admin/analytics


============================================================
48. API RULES
============================================================

All API requests must have:

Validation
Authentication where required
Authorization where required
Campus isolation
Consistent errors

Do not return unnecessary database fields.

Use response schemas.

Paginate large collections.


============================================================
49. FRONTEND DATA FLOW
============================================================

Use:

React component
↓
Feature hook
↓
API service
↓
FastAPI
↓
PostgreSQL

Use TanStack Query for server state.

Do not scatter fetch() calls across random components.


============================================================
50. ERROR RESPONSE
============================================================

Use consistent errors.

Example:

{
  "error": {
    "code": "RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND",
    "message": "Resource not found"
  }
}

Never expose stack traces.


============================================================
51. SECURITY
============================================================

Mandatory:

Secure password hashing
Authentication
Authorization
RBAC
Campus isolation
Rate limiting
Input validation
CORS
Secure headers
File validation
Request size limits
Audit logging
Secret management

Never:

Hardcode passwords
Hardcode API keys
Expose tokens
Expose database credentials
Trust frontend permissions
Trust frontend campus IDs


============================================================
52. REDIS
============================================================

Redis may be used for:

Caching
Rate limiting
Background jobs
Temporary state

PostgreSQL remains the source of truth.


============================================================
53. BACKGROUND JOBS
============================================================

Use background jobs for:

Notifications
Email
Analytics
XP processing
Search indexing
Cleanup

Do not overengineer job infrastructure.


============================================================
54. AI
============================================================

AI is optional within the MVP architecture.

If implemented:

Campus Assistant

Example:

"Find Python projects for me."

"Show CSE resources."

"What's happening this week?"

AI must only access authorized Campus OS information.

Never give an AI model unrestricted database access.

If no AI API key exists:

show a clean configuration state.

DO NOT fake AI.


============================================================
55. PERFORMANCE
============================================================

Implement:

Pagination
Lazy loading
Optimized queries
Database indexes
Image optimization
Caching where useful
Small API responses

Default pagination:

20 records approximately.

Never load thousands of records into one page.


