73. DEPLOYMENT READINESS
============================================================

Before final completion verify:

Frontend builds successfully.

Backend starts successfully.

Database migrations work.

Seed system works.

Environment variables documented.

Production build works.

No development secrets committed.

No broken routes.

No console errors.

No backend errors.

No fake API calls.

No dead buttons.

No missing pages required by MVP.

No unauthorized API access.

No cross-campus data access.

Docker works.

Tests pass.


============================================================
74. FINAL OUTPUT
============================================================

At the end provide:

1. Final architecture
2. Final file tree
3. Database schema summary
4. API summary
5. Environment variables
6. Local setup commands
7. Test commands
8. Build commands
9. Deployment instructions
10. Demo credentials using environment-based configuration
11. Known limitations
12. Future roadmap

Do not claim something works unless you actually tested it.


============================================================
75. MOST IMPORTANT RULE
============================================================

BUILD SMART.

BUILD CLEAN.

BUILD SMALL.

BUILD REAL.

Do not confuse complexity with quality.

Do not confuse more files with better architecture.

Do not confuse more features with a better MVP.

The objective is:

A COMPLETE
REAL
SECURE
RESPONSIVE
BEAUTIFUL
DEPLOYABLE
MAINTAINABLE
CAMPUS OS MVP.

HTML is mandatory.

CSS is mandatory.

JavaScript/TypeScript is mandatory.

React is the frontend framework.

Python/FastAPI is the backend.

PostgreSQL is the source of truth.

Use Tailwind for UI styling.

Use the minimum number of files and dependencies required.

Do not create unwanted files.

Do not create unwanted features.

Do not stop at the UI.

BUILD THE ENTIRE PRODUCT.
